From 0a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8f901234567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris McLaughlin <19711592+qBitnaut@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: ignore the vd55g infrared sensor

On the Surface Laptop 7 the qcom-camss media device carries two sensors:
the OV02C10 front camera and the VD55G0 infrared camera that
sl7-ir-bridge drives for face unlock. The simple pipeline handler
registered both, so a libcamera client (PipeWire through WirePlumber,
cam, a browser) that acquired the infrared camera enabled and streamed
its links, and the bridge then failed with "enable link: Device or
resource busy". The infrared sensor is not usable by the software ISP
anyway (mono, no tuning). Skip sensors whose entity name starts with
vd55g in locateSensors(), so the RGB camera is always camera 1.

Signed-off-by: Chris McLaughlin <19711592+qBitnaut@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index e26f438..c07cad3 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1782,8 +1782,24 @@
 	 * expose.
 	 */
 	for (MediaEntity *entity : media->entities()) {
-		if (entity->function() == MEDIA_ENT_F_CAM_SENSOR)
-			entities.push_back(entity);
+		if (entity->function() != MEDIA_ENT_F_CAM_SENSOR)
+			continue;
+
+		/*
+		 * Surface Laptop 7: the infrared camera (ST VD55G0, a mono
+		 * global shutter sensor on its own CSIPHY and CSID) is driven
+		 * by sl7-ir-bridge for face unlock. It is not a camera for the
+		 * software ISP, and a libcamera client that acquires it holds
+		 * the media links the bridge needs. Do not expose it.
+		 */
+		if (entity->name().compare(0, 5, "vd55g") == 0) {
+			LOG(SimplePipeline, Info)
+				<< "Ignoring infrared sensor '" << entity->name()
+				<< "'";
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		entities.push_back(entity);
 	}

 	if (entities.empty())
--
2.50.0
